{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810164-brainstorming-lupines-vs-kindred-in-nazi-germany","id":810164,"title":"Brainstorming: Lupines vs kindred in Nazi Germany","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-16T03:44:47-08:00","id":810164,"title":"Brainstorming: Lupines vs kindred in Nazi Germany","content":"One of the great things about these boards are that it's full of creative people, and I love bouncing ideas of you.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running a vampire campaign using the Transylvania Chronicles as the foundation, but also filling in some of the time gaps between chapters with other stories.<br /> <br /> Eventually, I'd love to set the story in Germany between 1920-1945, because, well, I think it's an absolutely fascinating time and place, thick with drama.<br /> <br /> The reason why I'm posting this here in the WtA section is that I'd also like to use this period as a backdrop to some good old fashioned vampire vs werewolf fighting.<br /> <br /> However, I don't know enough about the WtA line to come up with a motivation for lupines to get up in arms and start threatening the vampires of whichever city they are settled in, and was hoping for some ideas that would be reasonably compatible with WtA lore.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about the Wyrm (I'll look into it more as I flesh out a story outline), but is there any way it can be worked into something around Nazis and vampires? What tribes could you see getting involved?<br /> <br /> If you were brainstorming something along those lines, what angle would you approach it? Anything you guys can throw out there would be very appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T04:17:21-08:00","id":810169,"title":"","content":"I think White Wolf's original stance was that the Nazi regime and their crimes not supernaturally motivated.<br /> <br /> In general, there is a legend how werewolves think vampires came into existence and it amongst other reasons is a justification to kill them. In most cases, vampires do not cause that much misery and corruption that garou really care to hunt them explicitly - fomori, banes, black sprial dancers and the like are in general more dangerous to the general population and are therefore more often on the werewolves radar.<br /> <br /> But, in any case, if there are vampires and the werewolves stumble over their trail, they will still invest some effort to track them down and destroy them. It is a cultural obligation, rooted in their believe system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T06:10:20-08:00","id":810200,"title":"","content":"Yeah, i don't want some grand level supernatural conspiracy involving Nazis, but rather a local conflct.<br /> <br /> The problem is, although I understand that despite being natural enemies, werewolves and vampires generally keep to their own affairs... but that doesn't really serve my purposes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for the imput. I'll do some reading on the tribes you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T07:37:59-08:00","id":810223,"title":"","content":"I didn't mention any tribes, well one. Fomori are humans (or animals or supernaturals) possessed and fused with a bane (dark spirit). Banes are dark spirits and black spiral dancers are in fact a tribe of werewolves, who server the Wyrm - a cosmic embodiment of corruption and destruction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like I said, the garou don't keep to their own affairs, if they come across vampires. There really would have to be a direct bigger threat to let a vampire continue exist. But since you want the confrontation, just assume that there aren't any other threats the local garou have to deal with. If it is the 1920, then everything might be peachy for the german population - despite having lost the first WW. The war is over and the future is promising. In such a scenario the werewolves could very well decide, that it is time to hunt some vampires, since most other horrors they usually fight against are in hiding or beaten.<br /> <br /> If you want a more personal reason. Have a vampire kill or ghoul a person who is related to a local werewolf leader. While werewolves can't very well interact with humans, those humans who have werewolves in their ancestry can and form a kind of link between werewolves. They are the brothers, sisters, spouses, cousins and children of the local werewolves, and if a vampire even accidentally harmed one of them.... well, that might have been his last mistake...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T09:05:17-08:00","id":810254,"title":"","content":"In all honesty Werewolves are religious extremists that in all honesty put most existing terror groups or cults to shame. The only reason the average Werewolf needs to attack vampires is a humanity score below 6. In your theoretical scenario the Werewolves could have ignored the vampires until now i.e.1920's because the city was not large enough to threaten a Caern, but now the city's growth is expanding to include the Caern.<br /> <br /> Caern-a place of spiritual power for Werewolves and of huge interest to blood magicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T11:06:36-08:00","id":810295,"title":"","content":"Obviously, the Strain could give some ideas for Nazi / Vampire involvement. Even if they aren't the cause, it does present a lot of opportunity for the enterprising undead. (For feeding, and expanding territory and picking up retainers and herd.)<br /> <br /> Of course, if those attempts happen to cross into a Pack's turf and Kinfolk, hilarity ensues. (And flying body parts.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T12:43:27-08:00","id":810325,"title":"","content":"Well, to give something to work on, there was a schism in one tribe at the time. The Get of Fenris had some members who supported the Nazi ideals, and some who were against them. And as far as I know, they did fight over that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T14:13:31-08:00","id":810352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810164-brainstorming-lupines-vs-kindred-in-nazi-germany?p=810325#post810325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to give something to work on, there was a schism in one tribe at the time. The Get of Fenris had some members who supported the Nazi ideals, and some who were against them. And as far as I know, they did fight over that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent!<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a charismatic Garou buys into the Nazi ideals and joins the SS (their &quot;Blood and Soil&quot; ideology could be attractive to werewolves, I'd figure, which as per Wikipedia celebrated the &quot;relationship of a people to the land they occupy and cultivate, and it places a high value on the virtues of rural living&quot;). He becomes the commander of a secret unit of lupine fanatics.<br /> <br /> Taking it even further, as a parallel of Nazi racial beliefs, he leads his pack against the vampire parasites corrupting Germany, and when the Masquerade gets breached in the character's city, the incident brings the unit down on their heads. SS werewolf villains... yes. Just, yes.<br /> <br /> And then later, as the Third Reich crumbles around them, perhaps the characters will need to cover up the existence of this unit to protect the Masquerade, planting forged documentation to convince the Allies that 'Operation Werewolf' was nothing more than a plan for the Nazis to continue on with a guerilla war. Not sure about this one, but sounds fun, too.<br /> <br /> Anything else I should consider?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","user":"Blitzburger","date":". 01-16-2016, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T15:32:26-08:00","id":810379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810164-brainstorming-lupines-vs-kindred-in-nazi-germany?p=810352#post810352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excellent!<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a charismatic Garou buys into the Nazi ideals and joins the SS (their &quot;Blood and Soil&quot; ideology could be attractive to werewolves, I'd figure, which as per Wikipedia celebrated the &quot;relationship of a people to the land they occupy and cultivate, and it places a high value on the virtues of rural living&quot;). He becomes the commander of a secret unit of lupine fanatics.<br /> <br /> Taking it even further, as a parallel of Nazi racial beliefs, he leads his pack against the vampire parasites corrupting Germany, and when the Masquerade gets breached in the character's city, the incident brings the unit down on their heads. SS werewolf villains... yes. Just, yes.<br /> <br /> And then later, as the Third Reich crumbles around them, perhaps the characters will need to cover up the existence of this unit to protect the Masquerade, planting forged documentation to convince the Allies that 'Operation Werewolf' was nothing more than a plan for the Nazis to continue on with a guerilla war. Not sure about this one, but sounds fun, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that these guys still saw themselves as Gaian. That means they would have fought the corruption most of the Third Reich caused. While White Wolf made clear that no supernatural directly influenced the events, many of the Wyrm's forced (Fomori, Banes, Black Spiral Dancers) benefitted from them. And even these nazi-minded garou would have fought these, because its their duty to do so.<br /> <br /> They were all human born, most likely young men who grew in post-WWI germany. Their beliefs differed from the tribe thusly; They saw only white,male, human born garou are worthy. The rest of the tribe had no problems with women and respected their wolf born immensely. The racism thing is a bit more complicated, but most likely that wasn't true either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T15:32:54-08:00","id":810380,"title":"","content":"If you plan to use werewolves from The Apocalypse (not Masquerade Lupines, that's big difference), then maybe it's important to note that skinchangers are really nuts about racial purity and mumblings about The Golden Age and other that nonsense. Maybe some of more insane planned to use IIIrd Reich as a first step to rebuilding their beloved Impergium and to rule lesser race of man like cattle. The idea of lost German &quot;treasures&quot; being in part some supernatural werewolf mumbo-jumbo is quite appalling and very interesting. Werewolf packs destroying after the war any proof, witness and piece of truth about SS occult activities looks like something worth developing in whole WoD setting, not &quot;just&quot; a chronicle. Yeah, it's worth considering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10834-mictlantecuhtli","name":"Mictlantecuhtli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T15:44:19-08:00","id":810386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mictlantecuhtli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810164-brainstorming-lupines-vs-kindred-in-nazi-germany?p=810380#post810380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you plan to use werewolves from The Apocalypse (not Masquerade Lupines, that's big difference), then maybe it's important to note that skinchangers are really nuts about racial purity and mumblings about The Golden Age and other that nonsense. Maybe some of more insane planned to use IIIrd Reich as a first step to rebuilding their beloved Impergium and to rule lesser race of man like cattle. The idea of lost German &quot;treasures&quot; being in part some supernatural werewolf mumbo-jumbo is quite appalling and very interesting. Werewolf packs destroying after the war any proof, witness and piece of truth about SS occult activities looks like something worth developing in whole WoD setting, not &quot;just&quot; a chronicle. Yeah, it's worth considering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Yes, they are dogmatic, but the racial purity is less human race and more lineages of werewolves. So purebreed in the sense a certain dog is purebred, rather than any sort of skin colour/race is wrong. Some tribes don't even have breeding. During WW2, one camp did go for Nazi ideals. But only one camp in a large tribe.<br /> <br /> Impregrium is generally only wanted by one tribe, which is solely wolves. At the point of WW2, most of the garou nation has bred with humans long enough that they would not want to lose their human kinfolk to another Impegrium.<br /> <br /> As for being on the side of Nazi, that one camp (Sword of Heimindal) was in its way. But the rest? Actively fought against the taint that came from it in later days.<br /> <br /> Note that I'm not excusing the garou for any other sick shit they did. Just that they aren't like you describe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T15:52:18-08:00","id":810389,"title":"","content":"In the books - yes, it looks just like you explained. For the purposes of the story - what stays in the way of making Garou nation nothing more than purity obsessed, Impergium dreaming bunch of psychos with Germans as perfect tools for their agenda?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10834-mictlantecuhtli","name":"Mictlantecuhtli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T15:56:23-08:00","id":810391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mictlantecuhtli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810164-brainstorming-lupines-vs-kindred-in-nazi-germany?p=810389#post810389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the books - yes, it looks just like you explained. For the purposes of the story - what stays in the way of making Garou nation nothing more than purity obsessed, Impergium dreaming bunch of psychos with Germans as perfect tools for their agenda?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, of course. However, if the ST wants to use garou instead of lupines made into purity obsessed nazis, they should understand how the garou work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T20:22:05-08:00","id":810461,"title":"","content":"I don't imagine werewolves as being overly pro-Nazi or anti-Nazi. For us modern humans, the Nazis have an almost religious significance as the embodiment of evil. That wasn't the case in the 1930's or 1940's nor would it be the case for being with belief systems so radically different from our own as the Garou. So it is hard to imagine not caring that much, but I think that on average, werewolves would care more about the environmental or spiritual effects of the war than the ideology of the combatants. That isn't to say that some wouldn't care, but not as much as we might at first imagine.<br /> <br /> With a werewolf vs vampire conflict with the backdrop of WWII, it might be interesting to have Nazis versus non-Nazis and werewolves versus vampires be orthogonal conflicts. That is to say that some vampires support the Nazis and some oppose them, some werewolves support the Nazis and some oppose them. That could add some complexity to the situation if the players oppose both Nazis and vampires (which I am assuming here) and then have to either ally with Nazis to defeat some vampires or ally with vampires to defeat some Nazis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T22:00:55-08:00","id":810491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810164-brainstorming-lupines-vs-kindred-in-nazi-germany?p=810461#post810461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> With a werewolf vs vampire conflict with the backdrop of WWII, it might be interesting to have Nazis versus non-Nazis and werewolves versus vampires be orthogonal conflicts. That is to say that some vampires support the Nazis and some oppose them, some werewolves support the Nazis and some oppose them. That could add some complexity to the situation if the players oppose both Nazis and vampires (which I am assuming here) and then have to either ally with Nazis to defeat some vampires or ally with vampires to defeat some Nazis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, to be sure, I don't envision vampires as the innocent victims of Nazi werewolf oppression, as many of the NPCs would also have infiltrated and supported them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T14:11:36-08:00","id":811312,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mictlantecuhtli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810164-brainstorming-lupines-vs-kindred-in-nazi-germany?p=810389#post810389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the books - yes, it looks just like you explained. For the purposes of the story